  "decision": {
    "status": "approved",
    "rationale": [
      "The upgrade adopts modernc.org/sqlite v1.57.0 while retaining modernc.org/libc v1.74.4; its new defensive-mode behavior is opt-in and the project does not construct custom Driver instances.",
      "The reviewed BSD LICENSE and SQLite public-domain statement are byte-identical to the prior version, while the renamed LICENSE-SQLITE file is mapped to the exact new module version.",
      "The combined artifact profile retains the digest-pinned Node.js 24.19.0 frontend builder from main and a Node-free scratch runtime image.",
      "The optional modernc.org/sqlite/vec package and its separately hashed MIT license exist in the downloaded module but are not imported, linked, or copied into the scratch runtime artifact."
    ],
    "residualRisks": [
      "Importing modernc.org/sqlite/vec in the future would add sqlite-vec code and require the separately recorded LICENSE-SQLITE_VEC text, a new artifact review, and regenerated evidence before release.",
      "The new _defensive=1 mode rejects journal_mode=OFF, but this project does not enable _defensive and continues to generate only its reviewed _pragma DSN form.",
      "The new Driver registration API has a narrow behavior change for caller-constructed Driver values combined with vtab.RegisterModule; this project blank-imports the default driver and uses sql.Open instead.",
      "Passing the checked tests and vulnerability scan reduces but does not eliminate regression risk in the upgraded database engine."
    ]
  }
